comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T07:49:28.213Z","harness:codex","text=Duplicate check: searched all statuses for GH-915, Windows Node 24, /@id/D:/, preflight_ownership, release-automation npm log isolation, and SDK surface snapshot drift. Open pm-j668gl is the canonical broad Windows portability census and parent; no existing item owns this exact current-head multi-surface regression. Evidence: scheduled run 31077715874 and current-head dispatch 31081630028 reproduce the failure family."
  "2026-08-06T08:07:14.587Z","harness:codex","Evidence: current-head run 31081630028 proved stale restored Vitest transforms caused five missing suites plus stale assertion bytecode on Windows. Nightly and every CI test-bearing job now restore validation caches by exact content key only; the required Windows job includes every newly exposed SDK/release/activation suite. Focused contracts pass and full 6,888-test exact coverage plus static quality pass."
  "2026-08-06T08:16:29.627Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up evidence: PR #917 Windows job failed exact-tag recovery with status 128 because a native D:\\\\ temporary path was prepended to Bash PATH using a colon, bypassing the fake git and invoking real git.exe. The shared two-call shell fixture now converts FAKE_BIN with cygpath when available and preserves the shell inherited PATH. Both release and CI workflow contract suites pass (31 tests)."
  "2026-08-06T08:20:03.442Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first post-fix static-quality pass reached all deterministic gates but one SDK runtime import-cost sample measured 449ms over its 421ms ceiling; an immediate isolated rerun verified all 10 SDK entrypoints and all 6 CLI transport operations. No production source or entrypoint dependency changed in this follow-up."
  "2026-08-06T08:27:59.758Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up: accepted both CodeRabbit findings. All CI/nightly validation cache fingerprints now include Vitest-transformed scripts/*.mjs, scripts/**/*.mjs, scripts/*.mts, and scripts/**/*.mts inputs. The workflow contract parses YAML and structurally verifies all three CI validation-cache steps plus the nightly matrix step have no restore-keys fallback. Focused 12 tests and typecheck pass."
